[32m+[m[32m  1. Chains are session-scoped. agent-pi correlated across sessions, so one session's[m
[32m+[m[32m     `cat > /tmp/pr-body.md` plus another session's `chmod +x` became a "dropper".[m
[32m+[m[32m  2. Chains are entity-bound. A dropper needs the SAME path written, chmod'd, executed.[m
[32m+[m[32m     secret->exfil needs an actual egress command, not a docs WebFetch.[m
[32m+[m[32m  3. Each stage must match a DISTINCT event. agent-pi let one command satisfy two stages.[m
[32m+[m[32m  4. Substring matching replaced with anchored regexes ("cat /users" no longer matches[m
[32m+[m[32m     "cat /Users/me/bin/foo").[m
[32m+[m[32m  5. `git push` is medium, not high. Force push is high. Pushes are what agents do.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOptional model verdict for the gray zone sees METADATA ONLY (tool, args, recent actions,[m
